-# CurveYield vlSDT Liquid Locker V18.8 — Auditor Handoff (Uncompiled)
+# CurveYield vlSDT Liquid Locker V18.9 — Auditor Handoff (Uncompiled)
 
-V18.8 adds a dedicated cyGOV Yield Staking module, revises governance-token allocations, routes every protocol fee to Treasury except Revenue Staking's admin-role fee, and changes Revenue Staking's yield-over-benchmark split to 40% Treasury plus 10% admin.
+V18.9 resolves the two V18.8 audit findings without changing cyGOV reward top-up, reservation, or funding behavior.
 
-## Critical status
-
-This package has **not been compiled** by instruction. It has not received executable Solidity tests, exact runtime-bytecode measurement, fork simulation, deployment, or an independent security audit. Static checks are evidence only of source/package properties and cannot establish deployability or correctness.
-
-## New cyGOV Yield Staking
-
-`CurveYieldCyGovYieldStaking` accepts cyvlSDT and pays only cyGOV.
-
-- `targetYield`: cyGOV per 1e18 cyvlSDT per day, using 1e18 precision.
-- `maxMintRate`: maximum total cyGOV paid per day.
-- Max-rate backing: 30 days of free held cyGOV plus a protected Governance Token mint reservation.
-- Held cyGOV funds rewards before reserved mint capacity is consumed.
-- Accrued rewards become fully funded liabilities and are excluded from free backing.
-- Owner may mint only the still-unused part of the original 15B initial allocation into contract inventory.
-- Withdrawal fee: initial 2%, configurable 0–4%, paid to Treasury.
-- Daily decay: initial 3, configurable 0–10; one unit is 0.01% per completed day.
-- Decay is lazy, linear, interaction-triggered, and paid to Treasury.
-- Rate settings are immediate for seven days after deployment, then use a 14-day timelock.
-
-The protected reservation is included in `reservedByMinter`. A later allocation reduction cannot cut the minter below minted plus reserved usage. The Governance Token owner cannot directly cancel this protected reservation; the Yield Staking minter may replace or release it through its rate-setting flow. Immediate minter revocation remains an emergency shutdown surface for auditor review.
-
-## Governance allocations
-
-| Module | Initial cap | Maximum ongoing allocation |
-|---|---:|---:|
-| Revenue Staking | 5B cyGOV | 8% |
-| vlBoost Staking | 10B cyGOV | 12% |
-| cyGOV Yield Staking | 15B cyGOV | 30% |
-| Governance Staking Mint Controller | 20B cyGOV | 30% |
-
-Total initial allocation is 50B. Total ongoing allocation is 80%.
+## V18.9 changes
 
-## Revenue fee changes
+- Yield Staking decay now uses cumulative additive rate-seconds, producing the same principal for the same elapsed time regardless of checkpoint frequency.
+- Reward accrual is time-weighted over that same linear principal path so decay-driven emissions are cadence-independent.
+- Normal Revenue Strategy migration must claim, convert, and compound ordinary rewards or revert.
+- A separate emergency upgrade uses the same proposed strategy and seven-day delay, skips broken harvesting, returns principal, and permanently pauses/retires the old strategy.
+- Revenue Staking yield above benchmark now charges 33% to Treasury and 7% to the live admin-role address; 60% of excess remains in the staker flow.
+
+## Unchanged V18.8 systems
+
+- Held cyGOV is spent before reserved mint capacity.
+- Protected 30-day `maxMintRate` backing and automatic reserve top-ups.
+- 5B / 10B / 15B / 20B initial allocations and 8% / 12% / 30% / 30% ongoing allocations.
+- Yield Staking 2% initial withdrawal fee, 4% cap, daily decay rate 0–10, and 7-day setup plus 14-day rate timelocks.
+- Revenue Strategy 3.9% performance fee, 0.1% caller fee, and 0.1% withdrawal fee.
+- All protocol fees go to Treasury except Revenue Staking's 7% excess-yield admin fee; caller incentives remain caller payments.
 
-Revenue Staking rewards above the notifier-supplied benchmark are split:
-
-- 40% Treasury fee.
-- 10% admin fee.
-- 50% remains for active stakers.
-
-The 40% portion is transferred to Treasury. The 10% admin portion is transferred only to the address currently holding Revenue Staking's `admin` role. This admin fee is the suite's sole non-Treasury fee. Benchmark value represented by queued stake continues to be directed to Treasury separately.
-
-Revenue Strategy defaults remain:
-
-- 3.9% performance fee to Treasury.
-- 0.1% harvest caller fee to caller.
-- 0.1% withdrawal fee to Treasury.
-- Harvest-on-deposit enabled.
-
-Hard caps remain 9% performance, 1% caller, 1% withdrawal, and 10% combined performance plus caller.
-
-## Existing V18.7 architecture retained
+## Critical status
 
-- Beefy V7-derived Revenue Vault with stale-NAV-resistant deposits.
-- Seven-day vault strategy replacement.
-- Ten-day entire-converter replacement.
-- Immediate SDT-market and USDC route configuration inside the converter.
-- Dynamic Revenue Staking withdrawal-fee NAV and gross-up.
-- Separate cyGOV distributor for vault shareholders.
-- Slimmed Governance Staking with external Mint Controller and proposal-signature logic in the Governance Boost Strategy.
